<p>Dozens of miners died at a lead mining site in Nigeria’s Plateau state. Early accounts differ on what triggered the incident: some reports point to a carbon monoxide build-up or leak in underground tunnels, while others describe a gas explosion. Death tolls have been reported as “over 30”, at least 37, and at least 38. Multiple outlets said miners collapsed in poorly ventilated passages after gas accumulated, and authorities later recovered bodies from the site. Plateau state officials said injured survivors were being treated at nearby hospitals, and Nigeria’s mines ministry ordered the site shut after the incident.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Injuries and site detail: Arab News said the incident happened at a lead mine in Bashar, Plateau State, and reported 27 people were injured in addition to those killed. Local authorities said injured survivors were receiving treatment at nearby hospitals.</li><li>How early accounts were attributed: Reuters reporting cited by The Straits Times attributed the deaths to carbon monoxide poisoning, citing a police source and a security report. The BBC, meanwhile, quoted witnesses who described gas building up in poorly ventilated tunnels.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Witness accounts: Witnesses told the BBC that miners collapsed after gas built up in poorly ventilated tunnels. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwyk6nr80kxo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Security and police sources: A police source and a security report seen by Reuters described the deaths as carbon monoxide poisoning at the mining site. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/at-least-37-die-from-gas-inhalation-at-nigeria-mining-site'>The Straits Times (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Regional context: Al Jazeera said illegal mining is widespread in Nigeria and often operates without adequate oversight or safety protocols. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/19/at-least-37-killed-in-nigeria-mine-carbon-monoxide-poisoning-reports'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202602190111.html'>Nigeria: Explosion Kills Over 30 Miners in Plateau, Ministry Orders Mine Shut</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/at-least-37-die-from-gas-inhalation-at-nigeria-mining-site'>At least 37 die from gas inhalation at Nigeria mining site</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwyk6nr80kxo'>Suspected carbon-monoxide leak kills at least 30 miners in Nigeria, witnesses say</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/19/at-least-37-killed-in-nigeria-mine-carbon-monoxide-poisoning-reports'>At least 37 killed in Nigeria mine carbon monoxide poisoning: Reports</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.arabnews.com/node/2633518/world'>A gas explosion at a lead mine in Bashar, Plateau State, Nigeria, kills at least 38 miners working underground and injures 27 others.</a> - arabnews.com</li></ul>